            <div xml:id="d223">

                <pb facs="1038" n="1009" xml:id="pg1009"/>

                <head>223. National Security Decision Memorandum 184<anchor n="1" xml:id="d223-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1972-08-14">August 14,
                        1972</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <list type="to">
                    <item>TO <list>
                            <item>The Secretary of State</item>
                            <item>The Secretary of Defense</item>
                            <item>The Director, Office of Emergency Preparedness</item>
                            <item>The Secretary of Health, Education and Welfare</item>
                            <item>The Chairman, Atomic Energy Commission</item>
                        </list></item>
                </list>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <item>SUBJECT <list>
                            <item>United States Civil Defense Policy</item>
                        </list></item>
                </list>
                <p>The President has reviewed the Ad Hoc Group’s response to NSSM 57,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d223-f2"/> U.S. civil defense policy, and the views of the
                    interested agencies.</p>
                <p>The President has: <list>
                        <item>—Decided that the U.S. shall maintain the current overall level of
                            effort in its civil defense activities.</item>
                        <item>—Directed that there be increased emphasis on dual-use plans,
                            procedures and preparedness within the limitations of existing
                            authority, including appropriate related improvements in crisis
                            management planning.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Henry A. Kissinger</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
